          "date": "2026-10-29 22:05:16.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-29 23:14:45.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20565 tests: merge similar sanity-ec degraded-read subtests",
        "message": "LU-20565 tests: merge similar sanity-ec degraded-read subtests\n\nMany sanity-ec subtests ran the same create, write, resync and\ndegraded-read sequence and differed only in the file size, stripe\nsize, read offsets or the write before the resync.  Each repeated\nthe setup and the fault handling, and most hard-coded a 4+2 layout\nwith a gate of 6 or 8 OSTs, so they would be skipped on smaller\nconfigurations.\n\nMerge each group into one subtest that loops over the cases, and\nkeep the number of the subtest that remains:\n\n- 61a: sub-stripe, partial-stripe, partial-row and multi-row file\n  sizes with 64K, 256K, 1M and 4M stripes (42b 42c 46a 46b 46c\n  61b)\n- 58a: every pair of failed data OSTs, for 2+2 and for the default\n  layout when it has 2 parity stripes (43b 45b 45d 52a 68b)\n- 41a: aligned, unaligned and multi-row reads (41b 41c)\n- 70a: overwrite then resync: across a row boundary, unaligned,\n  after an extend, a partial row, either PFL component (67c 67d\n  70b 70c 70d)\n- 62a: staged, unaligned and sub-stripe appends (62b 62d)\n- 60a: truncate mid-stripe, to a row boundary, to 0, and before an\n  extend (60b 60c 73c)\n- 32a: OST stop and start, then write and resync, twice (30c 33a)\n- 34a: mirror resync, read and verify keep the size (34b)\n- 20: parity component layout and stripe size for 4M, 1M and 64K\n  stripes (1j)\n\nAdd ec_check_degraded() to read a file with the first, or each, data\nOST that holds no parity failed, and optionally two of them.\n\nThe merged subtests use EC_ARG, EC_DSTRIPE and EC_CSTRIPE and size\nfiles in rows of EC_DSTRIPE stripes, so they run with 3 OSTs (58a\nwith 4), and fail two OSTs only when EC_CSTRIPE >= 2.  Every\ndegraded read now compares the data with the healthy copy and\ndrops the client locks first: 41c read several ranges after one\ndrop_caches, 33a only checked that the read succeeded, and the\nsize of the unaligned appends in 62b was not checked.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ec\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I430d4648463a5e78d21c6a2dd58b4ce7b03ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
